\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces The unified curvature-based detection pipeline. Human (WritingPrompts) and machine texts from a generator $\phi $ form a balanced 500-document pool. A sampled document $x$ is masked (30\% of tokens in two-token spans) and refilled via a chosen strategy (dashed arrow) to yield 50 perturbed neighbours $x_i$. Detector $\theta $ scores $x$ and $x_i$, and the curvature $z(x) = \log p_\theta (x) - \overline  {\log p_\theta (x_i)}$ is thresholded into a decision. Each experiment varies one component while holding the rest fixed.}}{11}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{3.1}{11}{The unified curvature-based detection pipeline. Human (WritingPrompts) and machine texts from a generator $\phi $ form a balanced 500-document pool. A sampled document $x$ is masked (30\% of tokens in two-token spans) and refilled via a chosen strategy (dashed arrow) to yield 50 perturbed neighbours $x_i$. Detector $\theta $ scores $x$ and $x_i$, and the curvature $z(x) = \log p_\theta (x) - \overline {\log p_\theta (x_i)}$ is thresholded into a decision. Each experiment varies one component while holding the rest fixed}{figure.caption.3}{}}
